message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Liquid-biopsy-style partial observation maps for hybrid occult residual-disease modes"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Given a hybrid (switching) occult residual-disease model, which
  liquid-biopsy-style sparse observation maps can distinguish mode occupancy
  versus remaining blind to switches — as an observation-operator question,
  not as a diagnostic device claim? On a toy with an exogenous mode and a
  scalar count, quiescence and angiogenic pause share the count. A
  constant-coefficient map cannot see the switch between them. A two-channel
  turnover map on a coarse clock misses a short proliferative dwell. The same
  map on a fine clock recovers the switch times at a declared noise level and
  loses that recovery as false switches accumulate. Synthetic ctDNA-like
  series only. Not a validated assay. Not a medical device.
keywords:
  - observation operator
  - hybrid switching
  - liquid biopsy
  - ctDNA
  - occult residual disease
  - mode occupancy
  - toy model
  - identifiability
  - research-only
